# TU106 RTX 2070 (10de:1f07) --fuserows physical fuse-row capture, 2026-11-22
# ssdiag 0.8.8, --fusebase auto (turing -> 0x21000). First Turing physical
# row capture in the project; the 256-row hypothesis (6m) is now confirmed
# by data. IFF equivalent at the shifted base (0x21050) READS PLAIN:
# 0x00ff00b1 -> START=177, LAST=255 (256 rows) - the GA100-layout 0x820050
# is the blocked one; only CRC_STATUS is degraded on this base (badf at PL0,
# CRC guard off, announced). Two passes match (256 rows), address restored
# (FUSEADDR saved 255 == LAST). Explicit range 0x0-0xff requested.
# Provenance: user paste (Windows, elevated probe-driver run).
# CLASSIFICATION: UNKNOWN PER-DEVICE FUSE MATERIAL (standing, 2026-11-22).
# Rows 0x2a..0x47, 0x4b..0x57, 0x5a..0x5b, 0x5e are device-unique random material (byte entropy 89-100% of
# sample max after dedup; no decodable structure; sizes do NOT match any
# known public format incl. HDCP 1.x 280B / HDCP 2.2 RSA blocks, and differ
# per die). Entropy cannot distinguish secret keys from public verification
# material - both are random-looking by design - so the classification stays
# OPEN until an NVIDIA-side decode exists; HDCP was hypothesized but has no
# structural evidence. Anyone providing row dumps is informed of this
# classification in advance; sharing is optional, and these ranges may be
# redacted or withheld without losing analysis value (the fuse-pool records
# are the analysis-relevant part).
--- FUSE ROW DUMP (WRITE MODE) - writes: FUSEADDR row numbers + FUSECTRL CMD_READ only; no programming command; address restored after ---
